HoIP focuses on the course of COVID-19 infectious processes and cellular senescence. 

', 'Biological_Process;Dysfunction', 'OWL', 65, '2024/04/03', '2024-04-03T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOIP', 'ef9c4b0c0cec7051ee32d2045b7bd497cb905dd8728f7a624d1459846156b0cf', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 5.44, 5.44, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 6.18, 10.0, 7.905, 7.905, NULL, NULL, NULL, 317379, 14018, 14018, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:33:13+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HOM', 'Ontology of Homology and Related Concepts in Biology', 'This ontology represents concepts related to homology, as well as other concepts used to describe similarity and non-homology.', 'All_Organisms;Anatomy;Development;Molecule;Other', 'OWL', 7, 'releases/2015-01-07', '2022-01-12T18:06:11.000-08:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOM', 'ff83356bc7a45fb00fca09c6cc8a09e8987741b764c30afd2c0e3e7d76237db7', 'scored', NULL, 9.85, 6.58, 6.58, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 7.61, 9.0, 8.26, 8.26, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1098, 67, 67, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:05:15+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HOME', 'Health Ontology for Minority Equity', 'An ontology to record the physical, emotional and psychological effects resulting from differences in treatment that citizens receive based on their identity when entering healthcare institutions. We present the first version of such a Health Ontology for Minority Equity (HOME)', 'Health;Human', 'OWL', 1, '1', '2022-05-31T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOME', 'd174ecb8f10ca398c2528dd70f282d2686fbb38d00901e0dddb892154a21872f', 'scored', NULL, 9.28, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 6.05, 10.0, 6.3325, 6.3325, NULL, NULL, NULL, 469, 83, 83, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T06:04:37+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HOOM', 'HPO - ORDO Ontological Module', 'Orphanet provides phenotypic annotations of the rare diseases in the Orphanet nomenclature using the Human Phenotype Ontology (HPO). HOOM is a module that qualifies the annotation between a clinical entity and phenotypic abnormalities according to a frequency and by integrating the notion of diagnostic criterion. In ORDO a clinical entity is either a group of rare disorders, a rare disorder or a subtype of disorder. The phenomes branch of ORDO has been refactored as a logical import of HPO, and the HPO-ORDO phenotype disease-annotations have been provided in a series of triples in OBAN format in which associations, frequency and provenance are modeled.

HOOM is provided as an OWL (Ontologies Web Languages) file, using OBAN, the Orphanet Rare Disease Ontology (ORDO), and HPO ontological models.

HOOM provides extra possibilities for researchers, pharmaceutical companies and others wishing to co-analyse rare and common disease phenotype associations, or re-use the integrated ontologies in genomic variants repositories or match-making tools. ', 'Biomedical_Resources;Health;Human;Phenotype', 'OWL', 14, '2.6', '2018-03-08T12:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOOM', '7c011be7f165ba98b7fc8a2f728604580e611aeec2598d226fa51ecb4ac9777c', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 0.21, 0.21, 'same_as_strict', 0.0, 10.0, 5.0525, 5.0525, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3725403, 135862, 135861, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.1', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T22:05:00+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HOOM_V3', 'HOOM_New_Model', 'Orphanet provides phenotypic annotations of the rare diseases in the Orphanet nomenclature using the Human Phenotype Ontology (HPO). HOOM is a module that qualifies the annotation between a clinical entity and phenotypic abnormalities according to a frequency and by integrating the notion of diagnostic criterion. 

This new model of HOOM, used between ORDO and HPO is no more based on OBAN modelisation. It provides ORDO diseases concept annotated with HPO terms in a lightweight new dataset.', 'Biomedical_Resources;Health;Human;Phenotype;Vocabularies', 'OWL', 1, '3.0', '2025-12-09T15:12:56.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOOM_V3', '5cf1ec23081156bb022799f797c8afcb1d030587470057f7aef33be56b0f2d8c', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.0, 8.0, 4.5, 4.5, NULL, NULL, NULL, 509327, 120425, 4353, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T06:36:10+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HORD', 'Holistic Ontology of Rare Diseases', 'This ontology describes the bio-psico-social state of a person of rare diseses in a holistic way. It considers several contents such as disease, psychological, social, environmental state of the person.', 'Health', 'OWL', 4, '4.0', '2019-08-29T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HORD', 'cfdfc78f83f4aeb5d64e125586ab667aa4f2d74cb3675eb8baea4e2226229320', 'scored', NULL, 9.96, 0.01, 0.01, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.01, 10.0, 4.995, 4.995, NULL, NULL, NULL, 112711, 14613, 14558, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:22:58+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HOSP', 'Hospital Vocabulary', 'A RDF Schema that defines concepts and relationships used for Hospital data.', '', 'OWL', 1, 'v2015-09-30', '2015-09-30T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HOSP', '28a1576e97d89381e87401e937b1e7727625cd2bb70c9b49f5bd0807b24374f5', 'scored', NULL, 6.67, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.0, 4.0, 2.6675, 2.6675, NULL, NULL, NULL, 85, 9, 7, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T03:26:19+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HP', 'Human Phenotype Ontology', 'The Human Phenotype Ontology is being developed to provide a structured and controlled vocabulary for the phenotypic features encountered in human hereditary and other disease. Our goal is to provide resource for the computational analysis of the human phenome, with a current focus on monogenic diseases listed in the Online Mendelian Inheritance in Man (OMIM) and Orphanet databases, for which annotations are also provided. Please see documentation and license information at http://www.human-phenotype-ontology.org', 'Health;Human;Phenotype', 'OBO', 628, '2026-09-01', '2026-09-03T18:07:00.000-07:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HP', 'b672f59a93e5716efab044b788196a3bbd6e65bd707fb00ec401fb33729db308', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 4.82, 4.82, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 4.81, 10.0, 7.4075, 7.4075, NULL, NULL, NULL, 393535, 23928, 23928, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:38:44+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HPIO', 'Host Pathogen Interactions Ontology', 'Ontology for host pathogen interactions in farmed animals', 'Health', 'OWL', 2, '1', '2011-01-25T00:00:00.000-08:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HPIO', '8edfe0096a53f835a4d109f75438f7ef7fa784304d69e210fc1046577306a1e0', 'scored', NULL, 9.96, 6.26, 6.26, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 1.06, 9.0, 6.57, 6.57, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2316, 276, 276, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:06:09+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HPO', 'Hypertension-Ontology', 'The Hypertension Ontology, developed using the Protege tool, serves as a comprehensive knowledge framework for representing and organizing information related to hypertensive disorders. This ontology is designed to capture various aspects of hypertension, including its types, causes, and associated risks, with the aim of providing valuable insights for healthcare professionals, researchers, and policymakers. Leveraging the power of Protege, the ontology employs the OWL (Web Ontology Language) format to define classes, properties, and relationships, ensuring semantic clarity and interoperability. The taxonomy within the ontology encompasses a wide range of hypertensive conditions, allowing for detailed classification and representation. The ontology facilitates queries and exploration of hypertensive data through the use of the DL Query module in Protege, offering a practical tool for evaluating its usefulness. To enhance accessibility, the ontology is made available for download, enabling seamless integration into existing healthcare information systems. Its development involved a rigorous review of scientific literature and consideration of established methodologies, ensuring its alignment with best practices in ontology engineering. This Hypertension Ontology aims to contribute to the advancement of hypertension research, clinical practice, and healthcare decision-making.', 'Health', 'OWL', 1, NULL, '2023-12-02T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HPO', 'c6eba09ed0399482ab7be4775c4a0f6ce81c3b532d86ae15eda55acc0efdf20c', 'scored', NULL, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 2.11, 10.0, 3.0275, 3.0275, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1768, 276, 115, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T06:05:54+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HP_O', 'Hypersensitivity pneumonitis ontology', 'Hypersensitivity Pneumonitis Ontology involves the domain of knowledge of 1. diseases caused by organic dusts exposure including hypersensitivity pneumonitis as well as 2. organic dusts.', 'Other', 'OWL', 1, '1.0', '2018-07-17T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HP_O', 'd5f93bc5d2b75537601a10fdf48e1ca1b4457d355999d0e3c9a8643b21fc13fe', 'scored', NULL, 9.8, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 3.92, 10.0, 5.93, 5.93, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1306, 200, 200, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T03:26:19+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HRA', 'Human Reference Atlas', 'The Human Reference Atlas (HRA) is a comprehensive, high-resolution, three-dimensional atlas of all the cells in the healthy human body. The Human Reference Atlas provides standard terminologies and data structures for describing specimens, biological structures, and spatial positions linked to existing ontologies., The graph representation of the Human Reference Atlas (HRA) dataset.', 'Biomedical_Resources;Human', 'OWL', 12, 'v2.3', '2026-06-09T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HRA', '78c3a714133843c4c6fb67e1b26ceeb558e08f5576ceffc17891386f48f19368', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 0.19, 0.19, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.15, 10.0, 5.085, 5.085, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2158653, 187911, 12476, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T07:26:41+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HRAVS', 'HuBMAP Research Attributes Value Set', 'A collection of curated and standardized values used by the HuBMAP (Human BioMolecular Atlas Program) and SenNet (Cellular Senescence Network) metadata records to ensure uniformity in the description of samples and single-cell data produced by the consortium.', 'Vocabularies', 'SKOS', 202, NULL, '2026-09-21T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HRAVS', '6485a1fbbe6e3a6a4b305c85db5782caf1a3628629bb0b0edd64302b14ee874e', 'scored', NULL, 9.99, 5.05, 5.05, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.0, 0.0, 3.76, 3.76, NULL, NULL, NULL, 6857, 735, 734, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:07:58+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HRDO', 'Disease core ontology applied to Rare Diseases', 'This resource was designed during a PhD in medical informatics (funded by INSERM, 2010-2012). Its components are (i) a core ontology consistent with a metamodel (disorders and groups of disorders, genes, clinical signs and their relations) and (ii) an instantiation of this metamodel with Orphanet Data (available on http://orphadata.org).
</ br>
Research experiments demonstrated (i) efficient classifications generation based on SPARQL Construct, (ii) perspectives in semantic audit of a knowledge base, (iii) semantic comparison with OMIM (www.omim.org) using proximity measurements and (iv) opened perspectives in knowledge sharing (LORD, http://lord.bndmr.fr). 

Current production services of Orphanet developed ORDO, released in 2014, an ontology synchronized with their production database. This ontology is now available on Bioportal.', 'Health;Human', 'OWL', 2, 'V2', '2013-09-11T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HRDO', 'faf7cc246b86f3b7f307e7f52c0928527a2668bc6262219d708dec7906539da9', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 5.78, 10.0, 6.445, 6.445, NULL, NULL, NULL, 613614, 13540, 13540, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:39:59+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HSAPDV', 'Human Developmental Stages Ontology', 'Life cycle stages for Human. HsapDv was developed by the Bgee group with assistance from the core Uberon developers and the Human developmental anatomy ontology (EHDAA2) developers. Currently it includes both embryonic (Carnegie) stages and adult stages.

', '', 'OWL', 181, '2025-01-23', '2025-01-23T18:06:08.000-08:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HSAPDV', '81796e929a44f23a442faddee9702d660be0902bf0e6db264108c320c4d5011a', 'scored', NULL, 9.96, 6.99, 6.99, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 8.8, 10.0, 8.9375, 8.9375, NULL, NULL, NULL, 7090, 261, 261, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:07:23+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HSCLO38', 'Homo sapiens Chromosomal Location Ontology for GRCh38', 'HSCLO38''s purpose is to simplify the integration of genomic experimental data at different resolution scales within biomedical knowledge graphs. It defines chromosomal locations within the GRCh38 release for chr 1-22, X,Y and M.  HSCLO38 provides 3,431,153 classes at five distinct resolution levels: whole chromosome, 1 megabase pair (Mbp), 100 kilobase pairs (kbp), 10 kbp, and 1 kbp.  Each node within these class levels is interconnected to its scale parent and to the immediate neighbors on either side to support mapping and association between genomic datasets and features. For example, the 1kbp element HSCLO38:chr1.20517001-20518000 is_a connected to its "scale parent" HSCLO38:chr1.20510001-20520000 as well as to the 5'' neighbor HSCLO38:chr1.20516001-20517000 and 3'' neighbor HSCLO38:chr1.20518001-20519000.  We provide knowledge-graph-ready files for HSCLO38 on the project home page.', 'Biomedical_Resources;Genomic_and_Proteomic;Human', 'OWL', 4, NULL, '2024-02-12T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HSCLO38', NULL, 'failed', '{"errors":["No source file is available for this submission"],"status":404}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HSO', 'Health Surveillance Ontology', 'This is an ontology to support (one) health surveillance, focused on "surveillance system level data", that is, data outputs from surveillance activities, such as number of samples collected, cases observed, etc., An ontology to support semantic interoperability among domains involved in health surveillance (animal health, public health and food safety). More details at http://datadrivensurveillance.org.', 'Health', 'OWL', 10, '3.1.1', '2025-09-11T08:57:17.000-07:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HSO', '9dcabed1dffa2d3088f617308307131d9f9eb9dc73bc763f4ec425173b324390', 'scored', NULL, 9.98, 2.85, 2.85, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 2.2, 10.0, 6.2575, 6.2575, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12335, 640, 448, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:09:25+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HSPO', 'Health and Social Person-centric Ontology', 'The HSPO is an ontology that aims to represent and link together information about an individual from multiple domains. This work is motivated by the need to better understand the drivers of health outcomes that may arise from other domains including, but not limited to, the social determinants of health (e.g. ethnicity, transportation, education). This ontology can also describe a group of individuals that share similar characteristics (i.e. a cohort). Through this ontology we attempt to define a number of social contexts or social domains which can be useful to organise information coming from different terminologies such as ICD and SNOMED. 

Git Repository, Documentation and License details: https://github.com/IBM/hspo-ontology
Apache License 2.0', 'Health;Other', 'OWL', 3, '0.1.0', '2023-05-25T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HSPO', 'bc32d4d48db4ed72205f722fa32ad23664ffe1d32e0e7ac3f1bc30cfee966dfc', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 5.06, 5.06, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 4.67, 10.0, 7.4325, 7.4325, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2187388, 52661, 52461, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T07:28:43+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HTN', 'Hypertension Ontology', 'The Hypertension Ontology is a realism-based reference ontology for semantically managing clinical data about hypertension. Definitions of hypertension and elevated blood pressure are highly sensitive to context. Thresholds may vary according to population, guidelines, or clinical context. Variations in the clinical interpretation of blood pressure pose challenges to using blood pressure data for cohort identification, semantic data integration across data sets, and semantically enriching clinical data for clinical decision support applications. The Hypertension Ontology provides a framework for connecting clinical data to context-sensitive definitions of elevated blood pressure and hypertension.', 'Other', 'OWL', 1, NULL, '2019-05-20T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HTN', '0ef8e31c8c8cc36a21bc42cf038c012cfe543e2cc9f49679cbbcdf367c08afc2', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 4.46, 4.46, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 2.14, 9.0, 6.4, 6.4, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12078, 603, 603, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:09:20+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HTNCO', 'Hypertension Clinical Ontology', 'Hypertension Clinical Ontology is an OWL ontology designed to represent clinical knowledge related to hypertension. It includes concepts such as blood pressure classifications, hypertension types, symptoms, risk factors, biomarkers, complications, and treatment-related relationships. The ontology supports semantic organization, reasoning, and DL query-based exploration of hypertension-related biomedical knowledge.', 'Biomedical_Resources;Health', 'OWL', 1, NULL, '2026-06-22T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HTNCO', '4007e508f6888178a79ffff4905db3afcd0d4e0a69de2883470ec0ae03c25fd1', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.89, 8.0, 4.7225, 4.7225, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1179, 158, 158, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', NULL, '2026-09-23T06:05:17+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'HUPSON', 'Human Physiology Simulation Ontology', 'Large biomedical simulation initiatives, such as the Virtual Physiological Human (VPH), are substantially dependent on controlled vocabularies to facilitate the exchange of information, of data and of models. Hindering these initiatives is a lack of a comprehensive ontology that covers the essential concepts of the simulation domain. 
We propose a first version of a newly constructed ontology, HuPSON, as a basis for shared semantics and interoperability of simulations, of models, of algorithms and of other resources in this domain. The ontology is based on the Basic Formal Ontology, and adheres to the MIREOT principles.', 'Health', 'OWL', 1, '1.1.1', '2014-04-08T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HUPSON', '04535f284ba8fbd3379b487278c0fa7ce9f0000098c44aa3168838f31e6d47d9', 'scored', NULL, 10.0, 3.3, 6.57, 'http://scai.fraunhofer.de/HuPSON#SCAIVPH_00000009 [bioportal_definitionProperty + detected_by_name]', 1.08, 10.0, 6.095, 6.9125, NULL, NULL, NULL, 31385, 2933, 2920, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.1.1', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T22:57:24+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'I-ADOPT', 'I-ADOPT Framework Ontology', 'The I-ADOPT Framework is an ontology designed to facilitate interoperability between existing variable description models (including ontologies, taxonomy, and structured controlled vocabularies). One of the challenges in representing semantic descriptions of variables is getting people to agree about what they mean when describing the components that define the variables. The I-ADOPT ontology addresses this by providing core components and their relations that can be applied to define machine-interpretable variable descriptions that re-use FAIR vocabulary terms. This first version of the ontology has been developed by a core group of terminology experts and users from the Research Data Alliance (RDA) InteroperAble Descriptions of Observable Property Terminology (I-ADOPT) Working Group.', 'Other', 'OWL', 6, '1.1.0', '2025-05-28T18:06:36.000-07:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/I-ADOPT', '9f6dd6f48dd9f95bfa491dbf858e9052df34ca08d060beb48aa0e89181dade38', 'scored', NULL, 9.0, 5.65, 5.65, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 2.42, 6.0, 5.7675, 5.7675, NULL, NULL, NULL, 199, 10, 10, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:04:09+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ontology_scores (provider, acronym, name, description, categories, ontology_language, submission_id, version, released, bioportal_url, file_sha256, status, status_detail, describe_score, define_score, define_bp_score, define_bp_source, connection_score, flat_score, core_average, core_average_bp, logical_consistency_score, structural_dist_score, semantic_dist_score, triple_count, entity_count, class_count, wiseowl_version, core4_version, device, evaluated_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bioportal', 'I2SV', 'Integration and Implementation Sciences Vocabulary', 'Terms used to describe research concepts, methods and processes for addressing complex societal and environmental problems, especially investigations involving integration across different disciplinary and stakeholder perspectives, as well as implementation of findings into policy and practice change. The terms were originally developed for the Integration and Implementation Insights blog (http://i2Insights.org).', 'Other;Vocabularies', 'SKOS', 5, '1.0.0', '2021-04-14T00:00:00.000+00:00', 'https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/I2SV', 'e583b0aec59c33a1efa32050f91662140a2cd8146a9ad5b4aabe533e680b7b4f', 'scored', NULL, 9.95, 0.04, 0.04, 'same_as_strict (1.0 result, not re-checked)', 0.0, 0.0, 2.4975, 2.4975, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1333, 190, 189, '0.10.0', 'core4-1.0', 'cuda', '2026-09-23T06:05:46+00:00', '2026-09-23T23:25:10+00:00');
